# muyu 27 line — the XNU patch series actually applied to iPadOS 27.0.1 / 24A446.
#
# Referenced by board.spike27-live.toml (kernel.patch_series = ["device:patches/xnu/series-spike27"]).
#
# Provenance: this is the 72-entry list the 16:12 build of 2026-11-08 used, recovered from
# /tmp/spike27/patches/xnu/series-spike27 and cross-checked against the framework's own record of
# what it applied, /tmp/spike27-out/muyu/ipados-27.0.1-24A446/muyu-27/xnu-patches.list. The order
# is u159's order. Do not sort it: 67 of the entries are the shared xnu-12377 compatibility layer
# and their order matters at apply time.
#
# Why it had to be rebuilt: the file was declared by the board file and by porting.toml but had
# never been committed, and the loader does not fall back — patches.py raises
# "patch series missing" and the build stops. Every u-round was built from /tmp/spike27, whose
# copy of this file lived only in the temp tree. So the repo could not build its own 27 line.
#
# The two path forms:
#   os:../../../patches/xnu-12377/X.patch   resolves through the OS profile root to the framework's
#                                            own patches/xnu-12377 — the same relative hop the OS
#                                            profile series itself uses, so it works in both
#                                            UniXNU and UniXNU-27 checkouts.
#   X.patch                                  the five device patches, relative to this directory.
#
# Caveat, recorded rather than hidden: UniXNU/patches/xnu-12377 and UniXNU-27/patches/xnu-12377
# are not identical — offline-owner-boot-manifest, offline-owner-systemos-mount and
# zzz-boot-progress differ, and the UniXNU copies are the newer ones. So "os:" means "whichever
# framework you build against", and those three files make the two builds non-equivalent.
# scripts/audit-27-config.py reports the divergence; see porting.toml, configuration area.
#
# The five device patches are not grouped: four sit at the end (that is the order they were
# applied in), and sheng-platform-power.patch sits between the owner patches and zzz-boot-progress
# because the boot-progress patch depends on it. Leave the positions alone.
# Not in this series: patches/xnu/backlog/ — 16 patches copied from the 17 line (video console,
# last-panic replay, watchdog, the launchd traces) that never entered a 27-line build. They are
# the raw material for the screen re-plant in docs/SCREEN-ONLY.md §4; keep them out until that
# work starts, and add them here when it does.
#
# patches/xnu/wip/ is also absent on purpose: it is an archive of unfinished tree state, not an
# input to this series.

